/* book Worked example 2: Q: A rubber disc 80 mm in diameter and 10 mm thick (G = 0.8 MPa, k ≈ 1) is bonded to steel plates on both faces. Compare its stiffness in compression and in shear.
   1. Shape factor: S = 80/(4 × 10) = 2.
   2. E = 3G = 2.4 MPa; Ec = 2.4(1 + 2 × 2²) = 21.6 MPa.
   3. Area: A = π × 80²/4 = 5027 mm².
   4. Compression: kc = 21.6 × 5027/10 = 10 860 N/mm.
   5. Shear: ks = 0.8 × 5027/10 = 402 N/mm.
   Answer: The pad is 27 times stiffer in compression (10.9 kN/mm) than in shear (0.40 kN/mm). */
