/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Plot the engine torque against crank angle: this is the turning moment diagram.
   - Cs is the coefficient of fluctuation of speed; ω₁ and ω₂ the largest and smallest speeds; ω = (ω₁ + ω₂)/2 the mean speed in rad/s.
   - ΔE in J; I the mass moment of inertia in kg·m²; for a thin rim I ≈ mR², so ΔE = mv²Cs with v = ωR the rim speed in m/s.
   - The ratio ΔE / (work done per cycle) is the coefficient of fluctuation of energy Ce.
   - A solid disc of radius R and thickness b has I = ½mR² with m = ρπR²b.
   - σmax in Pa; ν is Poisson's ratio (about 0.25 for cast iron); ρ in kg/m³.
   - A rimmed flywheel puts most of its mass in a heavy rim joined to the hub by arms, so it gives about twice the inertia of a disc of the same mass and radius.
*/
