/* book Worked example 2: Q: An engine flywheel must handle ΔE = 15 kJ at 600 rpm with Cs = 0.02. Rim mean radius 0.6 m, radial thickness 120 mm, 6 elliptical arms, hub radius 0.1 m, cast iron ρ = 7200 kg/m³. The engine gives 50 kW. Find the rim mass and width, the rim stresses, and the arm size for a permissible stress of 15 MPa.
   1. ω = 2π × 600/60 = 62.83 rad/s; I = ΔE/(ω²Cs) = 15 000/(62.83² × 0.02) = 190 kg·m².
   2. Rim mass m = I/R² = 190/0.36 = 528 kg. Area = 528/(7200 × 2π × 0.6) = 19 440 mm², so width b = 19 440/120 = 162 mm.
   3. v = 62.83 × 0.6 = 37.7 m/s; σt = 7200 × 37.7² = 10.23 MPa.
   4. σb = 19.74 × 7200 × 37.7² × 0.6/(6² × 0.12) = 28.1 MPa.
   5. Combined: σ = 0.75 × 10.23 + 0.25 × 28.1 = 14.7 MPa.
   6. Torque T = 50 000/62.83 = 795.8 N·m; arm moment M = 795.8 × (0.6 − 0.1)/(6 × 0.6) = 110.5 N·m.
   7. a³ = 64 × 110 500/(π × 15) = 150 100 mm³, a = 53.1 mm; take a = 56 mm, b = 28 mm (σ = 12.8 MPa).
   Answer: Rim 528 kg, 162 mm × 120 mm; rim stress 14.7 MPa; arms elliptical 56 mm × 28 mm at the hub. */
